:scss
  $cyan: #0094ca;
  $light_cyan: #59b9dc;
  $lighter_cyan: #a6daed;
  $lightest_cyan: #d9eff7;

  .script_text textarea {
    field-sizing: content;
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .markdown {
    border: 5px solid gray;
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 10px;
  }

  .field.teacher-only-markdown {
    border: 5px solid gray;
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 10px;
  }

  #level_teacher_markdown_textarea_preview {
    border: 5px solid $cyan;
    background-color: $lightest_cyan;
    padding: 10px;
  }

%h1.control-legend{data: {toggle: "collapse", target: "#dsl_editor"}}
  DSL Editor

#dsl_editor.in.collapse
  .script_text
    = text_area_tag('level[dsl_text]', @level.dsl_text || @level.dsl_default)

    .markdown
      %p Edit Markdown:

      %textarea#level_markdown_textarea
      #level_markdown_textarea_preview

  - if @level.is_a?(BubbleChoice)
    %h4 Tip: Lab2
    %p
      By default, new levels use the more modern "Lab2" implementation of this level.
      You can add/remove the <code>uses_lab2</code> property above to control
      whether the level uses the modern or legacy versions of bubble choice levels.
      The Lab2 implementation can host non-Lab2 sublevels, but only transitions
      between Lab2 levels will be done without a page reload.
    %h4 Tip: Letters in bubbles
    %p
      If you are using the Lab2 version of bubble choice levels (described above),
      you can add/remove the <code>hide_letters_lab2</code> property above
      to control whether letters appear in the bubbles for each sublevel.
      The <code>hide_letters_lab2</code> has no effect on a legacy bubble choice level.
    %h4 Tip: Navigation Type
    %p
      The Lab2 version of bubble choice levels (described above) allows you to specify where a student should go after completing a sublevel.
      Use <code>navigation_type 'type_name'</code> to set the navigation type. Currently the following types are available:
    %ul
      %li
        <code>parent</code> (default): Clicking Continue on a sublevel returns to the parent bubble choice level. This is the default behavior if no navigation_type is set.
      %li
        <code>next_level</code>: Clicking Continue/Finish on a sublevel advances to the next in the level progression, or finishes the lesson if there are no more levels.
    %h4 Tip: Custom Modes
    %p
      With the Lab2 version of bubble choice levels (described above), certain custom modes
      are available which present alternate versions of the bubble choice level. Use
      <code>custom_mode 'mode_name'</code> to enable. Currently this includes:
    %ul
      %li
        <code>music_dance_ai</code>: A mode for Hour of AI 2025 which shows a custom
        tabbed experience where students can switch between a Dancer Creation, Music Creation,
        and Dance Creation level. At least one of these level types must be included as a sublevel
        for this mode to be enabled. If some sublevels are missing, the corresponding tabs will display
        as disabled and locked.

  - if @level.is_a?(Multi)
    %h4 Tip: Allow Multiple Attempts
    %p
      Set the <code>allow_multiple_attempts</code> property to <code>false</code> in the DSL
      to give students only a single opportunity to answer the question. By default, students
      are not allowed multiple attempts.

  - if @level.is_a?(External)
    %h4 Tip: Bubble Choice Options
    %p
      If this level will be a sublevel of a BubbleChoice level, you can set the following properties in the DSL:
    %ul
      %li
        <code>display_name</code>: The name of the level that will be displayed in the BubbleChoice.
      %li
        <code>bubble_choice_description</code>: The description of the level that will be displayed in the BubbleChoice.
      %li
        <code>thumbnail_url</code>: A URL to an image that will be displayed in the BubbleChoice.

  - if @level.is_a?(LevelGroup)
    %h4 Tip: Activity Guide Level
    %p
      Set <code>activity_guide_level</code> to <code>true</code> in the DSL to mark this
      level as an activity guide. For levels with this setting enabled, the submission
      dialog traditionally shown for LevelGroups will not render, allowing the level to
      behave more like a standard in-progression level.

  - if @level.is_a?(Match) || @level.is_a?(Multi)
    %h4 Tip: Height Tags
    %p
      You can change the height of any attribute (e.g., MC, Match) by adding
      <code>height 'XXX'</code> under the name of the level in the DSL.
      Note that this applies to all items in the level and cannot be set for individual items.

// Don't not use the _teacher_only_markdown.haml partial for DSL levels because they need
// extra functionality (initializeEmbeddedMarkdownEditor) to save the markdown content into the level file
- unless @level.is_a?(EvaluationMulti)
  %h1.control-legend{data: {toggle: "collapse", target: "#teacher_only_markdown"}}
    Teacher Only Markdown

  #teacher_only_markdown.in.collapse
    .field.teacher-only-markdown

      %textarea#level_teacher_markdown_textarea
      #level_teacher_markdown_textarea_preview
